            <ArticleTitle>Pd-Catalyzed Diastereoselective Trifluoromethylthiolation of Functionalized Acrylamides.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5106-5109</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02384</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Pd-catalyzed diastereoselective trifluoromethylthiolation of acrylamides was developed to allow the formation of the Z-isomer as a single product. Using a C-H bond functionalization strategy, the method was applied to a broad range of α-aryl, α-alkyl, and α,β-disubstituted acrylamides bearing the amide derived from the 8-aminoquinoline as a directing group. Mechanistic studies as well as postfunctionalization of the products were performed. This approach opens new routes to unprecedented SCF3-containing scaffolds.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
